{"title":"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f72854961d8a9472daefd47b0b089867605b429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,\\cdots, 1998\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> has been partitioned into disjoint pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f64870b76e16d812d79938c0f7bd59426e8c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_i,b_i\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b836c8edc0bdd0fcc8467756a26406902d1657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i\\leq 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />) so that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b88963fc9f7c4fa923c59d185083d05b54103cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_i-b_i|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/8/c986d59da1a579f6d783633ebe60315bc9ede782.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a_1-b_1|+|a_2-b_2|+\\cdots +|a_{999}-b_{999}|\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"18\" /> ends in the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/2709f7adfba977c9c5cc8d138745e93ca33cc3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_i - b_i| \\equiv 1 \\pmod 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92ccb2146c24e36a78f944a4f2303cf98701f516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=|a_1-b_1|+|a_2-b_2|+\\cdots +|a_{999}-b_{999}| \\equiv 1+1+\\cdots + 1 \\equiv 999 \\equiv 4 \\bmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"622\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Also, for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec00004a5113b974f70a8e26c3781261e56464e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2ba9ffb951ec4349f583c9893539e612c21a5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|M-N| \\equiv M-N \\equiv M+N \\bmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"287\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d15c109e247ef70c2d0e3facf680ef09507db1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\equiv a_1+b_1+a_2+b_2+\\cdots +a_{999}+b_{999} \\equiv 1+2+ \\cdots +1998 \\equiv 999*1999 \\equiv 1 \\bmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"673\" height=\"15\" /> also, so by the Chinese Remainder Theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b268cb7e21043a8508c8a91b0705c8e19e47d4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\equiv 9\\bmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> ends in the digit 9, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>FASTEST SOLVE ON STREAM from v_Enhance (:omighty:)\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jsw3c3yAn7o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jsw3c3yAn7o</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO\" title=\"1998 USAMO\">1998 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017024054\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 120/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1284/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3102/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time